---
// The no-flash path, replacing Starlight's.
//
// Byte-for-byte the script BaseLayout runs, and for the same reasons: a theme
// applied after first paint is a white flash on a warm-near-black page, so
// the stored choice is written onto <html> before any stylesheet is parsed.
// It cannot be a module and cannot be deferred.
//
// Absent a stored choice, nothing is written and the CSS falls through to
// prefers-color-scheme. Three states -- explicit dark, explicit light, and
// "follow the system" -- with the absent attribute as the third rather than a
// fourth value to keep in sync. Starlight's own provider always writes an
// explicit value, which is the one behaviour this has to replace.
//
// Starlight's version also exposed `window.StarlightThemeProvider` for its
// picker to call. Nothing references it once ThemeSelect is overridden too.
---

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    try {
      var stored = localStorage.getItem("ripen-theme");
      if (stored === "dark" || stored === "light") {
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = stored;
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>
